Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?patch:=20installer-reinstall-empty-list=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20treat=20leftover=20'[]'=20as=20empty=20patch=20laye?=
 =?UTF-8?q?r?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

uninstall() leaves '[]' in $DSH_HOME/cordis.patch.yml (dsh requires a
top-level array); install() then treated that scalar as user content and
concatenated its marker block after it — a scalar followed by sequence
entries is invalid YAML and crash-loops dsh-web on boot.

Observed in production 18.09.2026: skillsync reinstall produced
'[]\n\n# HINDSIGHT_CODING_AGENTS_DSH_START...' pointing at a dead
file:///tmp path; dsh-web crash-looped until the file was repaired by hand.

Regression test: install → uninstall → install round trip.
---
 .../coding-agents/src/installer.test.ts             | 13 +++++++++++++
 .../coding-agents/src/installer.ts                  |  6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hindsight-integrations/coding-agents/src/installer.test.ts b/hindsight-integrations/coding-agents/src/installer.test.ts
index 80d85afeb..8f238a839 100644
--- a/hindsight-integrations/coding-agents/src/installer.test.ts
+++ b/hindsight-integrations/coding-agents/src/installer.test.ts
@@ -724,6 +724,19 @@ describe("dsh installer", () => {
     expect(readFileSync(patchPath(ctx), "utf8").trim()).toBe("[]");
   });
 
+  it("re-install after uninstall does not glue our block onto the leftover '[]'", () => {
+    const ctx = makeCtx();
+    run(["install", "dsh"], ctx);
+    run(["uninstall", "dsh"], ctx);
+    expect(readFileSync(patchPath(ctx), "utf8").trim()).toBe("[]");
+    run(["install", "dsh"], ctx);
+    const patch = readFileSync(patchPath(ctx), "utf8");
+    // "[]" is a scalar: a sequence entry after it is invalid YAML, and dsh fails BOOT on this
+    // file. The leftover must be treated as an empty patch layer, not as content to keep.
+    expect(patch.trim().startsWith("[]")).toBe(false);
+    expect(patch.match(/- id: hindsight/g)).toHaveLength(1);
+  });
+
   it("uninstall keeps the user's own patches", () => {
     const ctx = makeCtx();
     run(["install", "dsh"], ctx);
diff --git a/hindsight-integrations/coding-agents/src/installer.ts b/hindsight-integrations/coding-agents/src/installer.ts
index 2e78e6cda..2477d1d71 100644
--- a/hindsight-integrations/coding-agents/src/installer.ts
+++ b/hindsight-integrations/coding-agents/src/installer.ts
@@ -1619,7 +1619,11 @@ const dsh: HarnessInstaller = {
     const existing = existsSync(path) ? readFileSync(path, "utf8") : "";
     // REPLACE any previous block rather than skipping: a re-install after the package moved must
     // repair the now-dead path, which is exactly what `install` is for.
-    const others = existing.replace(DSH_BLOCK_RE, "\n").trim();
+    const stripped = existing.replace(DSH_BLOCK_RE, "\n").trim();
+    // A previous UNINSTALL leaves "[]" behind (dsh requires a top-level array, see uninstall).
+    // That is an empty patch layer, not content: concatenating our block after it yields a scalar
+    // followed by sequence entries — invalid YAML that crash-loops the host on boot.
+    const others = stripped === "[]" ? "" : stripped;
     const entry = pathToFileURL(join(c.dist, "dsh.js")).href;
     const block =
       `${DSH_MARKER_START}\n` +
